WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.191
Good morning, Hank, it's Friday.

00:00:01.191 --> 00:00:04.920
It's actually Thursday, but tomorrow I'm going
to be in airports all day.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.620
Now I know what you're saying, Hank: "But
John, I can tell by the gray speckled behind

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.420
you that you are currently in an airport".

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.930
That's true, but today I'm just in two airports.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.920
Tomorrow I'm going to be in a ton of them.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.780
Ugh boy, I am the sleepiest sleepyhead in
Sleepslvania.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.640
Do I have the vague resemblance of a Harry
Potter scar drawn on my forehead?

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.640
No apologies.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.110
So, Hank, today is the last day of pizzamas,
which means it is the last day that you can

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.510
buy any of these things with my mustachio-ed
face on them.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.170
So if you want a glow-in-the-dark Pizza John
shirt or a David Bowie Pizza John shirt or

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.600
if you want to dress your baby in a Pizza
John onesie, today is the last day.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.060
Link in the dooblydoo.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.410
In other news, I'm very, very tired.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.520
Cara Delevingne, Nat Wolff and I did our modeling
faces yesterday.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.030
Hank, we've all been practicing our model
faces, Cara has a pretty good one.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.899
It's so funny!

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:55.879
I can't-- it's so great!

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:57.730
Alright, Nat has a pretty good one.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:58.730
Nat: Normal.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:00:59.730
(everybody laughs)

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.730
John: No!

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.850
It's better when you try, it's better when
you try.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.039
Your sincere model face.

00:01:06.039 --> 00:01:07.929
Nat: I can't do the cheek thing.

00:01:07.929 --> 00:01:09.179
Cara: No, you just suck it in.

00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:10.179
John: No.. you-u-you-op..

00:01:10.179 --> 00:01:11.179
Nat: What do I do?

00:01:11.179 --> 00:01:12.180
John: You open your mouth a little bit...

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.469
(laughter) THAT ONE!

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:17.673
That one is a good one!

00:01:17.673 --> 00:01:18.673
Nat: Was it really good?

00:01:18.673 --> 00:01:19.673
John: No!

00:01:19.673 --> 00:01:20.673
So this is my normal face.

00:01:20.673 --> 00:01:21.673
And this is my model face..

00:01:21.673 --> 00:01:22.673
like...

00:01:22.673 --> 00:01:23.673
Nat: So subtle.

00:01:23.673 --> 00:01:24.673
Yeah!

00:01:24.673 --> 00:01:25.673
Cara: I like the soft attitude.

00:01:25.673 --> 00:01:28.959
John: Hank, everyone involved in the Paper
Towns movie is doing such a great job, and

00:01:28.959 --> 00:01:32.619
I don't know how they do it, because the hours
are incredibly long.

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:37.241
Like, all I'm doing is like sitting in a chair,
eating peanut M&amp;Ms, laughing and crying, as

00:01:37.241 --> 00:01:40.439
all these hardworking people bring this story
to life.

00:01:40.439 --> 00:01:46.409
And yet, despite the ridiculous easiness of
my job, I am truly the most fatigued, fatigued

00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:47.819
person in all of Fatiguedville.

00:01:47.819 --> 00:01:51.689
So anyway, thank you to everyone in the Paper
Towns crew who's going to stay up until five

00:01:51.689 --> 00:01:56.630
o'clock in the morning tonight, because that
is... oh boy, I don't know how you're going

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:57.630
to do it.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.810
Oh, Nerdfighters, I also want to say thanks
for your feedback on Project for Awesome 2014,

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.899
I will talk more about that when I'm not the
most exhausted exhaustee in all of Exhaustia.

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:07.110
And Hank, I also wanted to say that I really
enjoyed Pizzamassing with you.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.689
It's made me feel like uhh..

00:02:09.689 --> 00:02:10.689
I don't know!

00:02:10.689 --> 00:02:13.340
It's just been really fun.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:14.760
Good ol' days kind of feeling.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.950
You know what would also be fun, Hank?

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:16.950
Going to sleep!

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.370
And fortunately, I'm about to be on a giant
steel cylinder that will hurtle hundreds of

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:25.040
miles through the thin and unsurvivable atmosphere,
30,000 feet above sea level.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.750
And that's just the kind of environment I'd
like to sleep in.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:28.750
Oookay Hank!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.870
I didn't really believe in myself, but I did
get some sleep on the flight, now I am in

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:33.870
Los Angeles.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.579
Earlier today, I got to be with Shailene Woodley
and Ansel Elgort and lots of other people

00:02:37.579 --> 00:02:38.939
involved in The Fault in our Stars movie.

00:02:38.939 --> 00:02:42.430
As an Amsterdam-esque Fault in our Stars bench
was installed on the Fox lot.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:48.250
The Fox lot has a statue of Napoleon Dynamite
and murals of The Simpsons and Star Wars...

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.859
and to join that kind of company is just uhh..

00:02:51.859 --> 00:02:52.859
It's pretty wonderful.

00:02:52.859 --> 00:02:57.920
And now, I am going to go to bed-- is what
I would like to say, but in fact, I am going

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.079
to go to the airport.

00:02:59.079 --> 00:03:00.579
Hank, you'll see me on Tuesday.

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:06.370
P.S, Nerdfighters, the AFC Wimbly Womblies
have just played the most important games

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.609
in their history!

00:03:07.609 --> 00:03:09.489
Link's in the doobly doo!

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.180
Or you can click overr...

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.879
here...

